  "id": "DrugBank_DB06005 - MONDO_809",
  "verbalization": "Adomiparin is associated with Purpura Fulminans through a chain of indications that link it to Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC), a condition characterized by widespread microvascular thrombosis and bleeding. This connection is supported by the shared indication of DIC with Adomiparin, Heparin, and Dalteparin, all of which are anticoagulants. The evidence suggests that Adomiparin may exert a therapeutic effect by modulating the coagulation cascade, potentially mitigating the excessive clotting seen in DIC. The presence of multiple anticoagulant agents with similar indications for Purpura Fulminans implies a broader role in the pathophysiology of the condition, possibly through mechanisms involving anti-inflammatory or antithrombotic actions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Adomiparin to be repurposed for the treatment of DIC and its complications, based on its established role in managing coagulation disorders.",
